{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01OA:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01OA", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nBy Modules, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe symmetric algebra <MATH_0004> of\n<MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>\nis a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0007>-algebras.\nNote that it is generated in degree <MATH_0008> over <MATH_0009>.\nHence it makes sense to apply the construction of the\nprevious section to it, specifically Lemmas\n<REF_0002> and <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-whole-tensor-algebra-permanence}", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0008": "$1$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-relative-proj}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-apply-relative}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f3a5888e9ff66fddefa1f3dedf65517e869bf4722571d60c820bf4a1d7b31151", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c0400f269d5ccee81784fce819586ce52ee695e27d8c0137ba2c38d31e2b2bc", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a27720886b2061c8a981495b6ee635871cdf69479f5c389d41544e01388c767"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01OB:statement", "parent_tag": "01OA", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-module<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>The reader may expect here\nthe condition that <MATH_0004> is finite locally free. We do not\ndo so in order to be consistent with\n<REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\nWe denote\n<MATH_0005>\nand we call it the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>projective bundle associated to <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nThe symbol <MATH_0007>\nindicates the invertible <MATH_0008>-module\nof Lemma <REF_0002> and is called the <MATH_0009>th\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>twist of the structure sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "REF_0001": "\\cite[II, Definition 4.1.1]{EGA}", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\pi :\n\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) = \\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{E}))\n\\longrightarrow\nS\n$$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(n)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-apply-relative}", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-projective-bundle}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:a80b818318181c533e6242d09cea7a793b94537cd2f57ce894bf2ac5b7ef8050", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91ac564543202fece4a0d466ef4bb8035f9fe5ffa5c6fd5fcc387e333c0a2e7a", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67ac7fca357404876eddc9f8ae1ea5fa920881956580958a11f2cf44ef7030c7"}
{"schema_version": 2, "unit_id": "tag:01OA:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "01OA", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAccording to Lemma <REF_0001> there are\ncanonical <MATH_0001>-module homomorphisms\n<MATHSEG_0001>equivalently<MATHSEG_0002>\nfor all <MATH_0002>. In particular, for <MATH_0003> we have\n<MATHSEG_0003>equivalently<MATHSEG_0004>\nand the map <MATH_0004>\nis a surjection by Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThis is a good way to remember how we have normalized\nour construction of <MATH_0005>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nWarning: In some references the scheme <MATH_0006>\nis only defined for <MATH_0007> finite locally free on <MATH_0008>.\nMoreover sometimes <MATH_0009> is actually defined as our\n<MATH_0010> where <MATH_0011>\nis the dual of <MATH_0012> (and this is done only when <MATH_0013> is\nfinite locally free).\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nLet <MATH_0014>, <MATH_0015>, <MATH_0016> be as in\nDefinition <REF_0003>. Let <MATH_0017>\nbe a scheme over <MATH_0018>. Let <MATH_0019>\nbe a surjection where <MATH_0020> is an invertible <MATH_0021>-module.\nThe induced graded <MATH_0022>-algebra map\n<MATH_0023>\ncorresponds to a morphism\n<MATH_0024>\nover <MATH_0025> by our construction of the relative Proj as the scheme representing\nthe functor <MATH_0026> in Section <REF_0004>. On the other hand,\ngiven a morphism <MATH_0027> over <MATH_0028>\nwe can set <MATH_0029>\nand <MATH_0030> equal to the pullback\nby <MATH_0031> of the canonical surjection\n<MATH_0032>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0005> these constructions\nare inverse bijections between the set of isomorphism classes of pairs\n<MATH_0033> and the set of morphisms\n<MATH_0034> over <MATH_0035>.\nThus we see that <MATH_0036> represents the functor\nwhich associates to <MATH_0037> the set of <MATH_0038>-module\nquotients of <MATH_0039> which are locally free of rank <MATH_0040>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-relative-proj-twists}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\text{Sym}^n(\\mathcal{E})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(n)\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\pi^*\\text{Sym}^n(\\mathcal{E})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(n)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$n \\geq 0$", "MATH_0003": "$n = 1$", "MATHSEG_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{E}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(1)\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "}\\quad\n\\pi^*\\mathcal{E}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(1)\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi^*\\mathcal{E} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(1)$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-apply-relative}", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}^\\vee)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{E}^\\vee$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "MATH_0014": "$S$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\to S$", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-projective-bundle}", "MATH_0017": "$f : T \\to S$", "MATH_0018": "$S$", "MATH_0019": "$\\psi : f^*\\mathcal{E} \\to \\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{O}_T$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{O}_T$", "MATH_0023": "$$\nf^*\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{E}) = \\text{Sym}(f^*\\mathcal{E}) \\to\n\\text{Sym}(\\mathcal{L}) = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}\n$$", "MATH_0024": "$$\n\\varphi_{\\mathcal{L}, \\psi} : T \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})\n$$", "MATH_0025": "$S$", "MATH_0026": "$F$", "REF_0004": "\\ref{section-relative-p